OL,3,GNEWSA'I couldn't move, walk or talk
OL,4,Aafter my stroke'
OL,5,
OL,6,FA former primary school teacher said
OL,7,Fher "life has changed beyond belief"
OL,8,Fafter having a stroke in 2019.
OL,10,FPriscilla Zuta, from Wisbech,
OL,11,FCambridgeshire, was 42 when she had a
OL,12,Fstroke in 2019, which left her with
OL,13,Fright-sided weakness and aphasia, a
OL,14,Fcondition that affects communication.
OL,16,FZuta, now 48, has shared her experience
OL,17,Fon World Stroke Day as part of a
OL,18,Fcampaign by the Stroke Association,
OL,19,Fwhich aims to raise awareness of the
OL,20,Fcondition's prevention, symptoms,
OL,21,Ftreatment and survivor support.
OL,23,APub: 29-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
